(ned ROTARY ZERO -- find the B chuck axis with a round bar and the tool at hand)
(Operator 2026-08-11: "i will always put the same stick of aluminum in for this)
(purpose ... start close to the top ... find zero by touching Z with the tool at)
(hand, then go X- by diameter of tool going down by 1in and probe X+, then repeat)
(moving X+ and probing X-. centre in X is the midpoint. the bar is 1.25in.")
(X CENTRE IS THE MIDPOINT AND THE TOOL RADIUS CANCELS: the left touch stops with)
(the tool flank on the bar at x_left+R, the right touch at x_right-R, so the mean)
(of the two RAW touches is the axis regardless of what tool is in the spindle.)
(THE X MIDPOINT IS VALID AT ANY DEPTH -- a circle is symmetric about its centre)
(line, so the side probes do not care that they are below the crown.)
(Z IS NOT A MIDPOINT: only the crown is reachable, so the axis is one bar RADIUS)
(below the top touch. That makes the bar diameter the one number this routine)
(has to be told, and a wrong one puts Z0 wrong by half the error, silently.)
(PROBE CIRCUIT. G38 senses motion.probe-input, which on ned is the toolsetter)
(contact: 7I84 input-28 via R10, whose coil sits between +24V and node *87 -)
(docs/tracing/relays.md:270-278. The return is chassis ground through the)
(spindle, so the sensed thing must be ON *87 and insulated from the frame.)
(Operator 2026-08-11: 'the bar will be electrically identical to the)
(toolsetter' - so the bar is on *87 and this works as written. If the bar is)
(ever left at chassis ground instead, tool-to-bar is ground-to-ground, the)
(coil never sees current, and the tool drives in until a limit. The o90 gate)
(proves the circuit is OPEN before committing, which catches a shorted or)
(already-touching lead; it cannot prove the clip is on the right metal, so)
(the first Z touch is still the one to stand ready on.)
o<rotary_zero> sub
  #<bar_dia>   = #1
  #<depth>     = #2
  #<max_z>     = #3
  #<max_x>     = #4
  #<f_fast>    = #5
  #<f_slow>    = #6
  #<f_trav>    = #7
  #<clear>     = #8
  o10 if [#<bar_dia> LE 0]
    #<bar_dia> = 31.75
  o10 endif
  o11 if [#<depth> LE 0]
    #<depth> = 25.4
  o11 endif
  o12 if [#<max_z> LE 0]
    #<max_z> = 40.0
  o12 endif
  o13 if [#<max_x> LE 0]
    #<max_x> = 40.0
  o13 endif
  o14 if [#<f_fast> LE 0]
    #<f_fast> = 100.0
  o14 endif
  o15 if [#<f_slow> LE 0]
    #<f_slow> = 10.0
  o15 endif
  o16 if [#<f_trav> LE 0]
    #<f_trav> = 500.0
  o16 endif
  o17 if [#<clear> LE 0]
    #<clear> = 3.0
  o17 endif
  #<r_bar> = [#<bar_dia> / 2.0]
  (the tool must be a known one: the X clearance moves are its own diameter)
  o20 if [#5400 LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: no tool in the spindle - it is the probe here)
  o20 endif
  #<t_dia> = #5410
  o21 if [#<t_dia> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: tool #5400 has no diameter in the table)
  o21 endif
  (the probe depth must actually be ON the bar, or the side probes miss it)
  o22 if [#<depth> GE #<bar_dia>]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: probe depth is at or below the bottom of the bar)
  o22 endif
  (HALF-WIDTH AT THE PROBE DEPTH, not the radius: the side probes land below the)
  (crown, where the bar is narrower. h = sqrt of r^2 minus r-depth squared.)
  #<h> = [SQRT[[#<r_bar> * #<r_bar>] - [[#<r_bar> - #<depth>] * [#<r_bar> - #<depth>]]]]
  o23 if [#<h> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: probe depth gives no material to touch)
  o23 endif
  (CIRCUIT MUST BE OPEN BEFORE WE MOVE. A probe already made looks identical to)
  (a probe that trips instantly, and G38.2 would return the start point as a)
  (touch -- a silent wrong answer is worse than a refusal.)
  M66 P2 L0
  o90 if [#5399 LT 0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: cannot read the probe input)
  o90 endif
  G92.1
  G90
  (1. TOP OF THE BAR. Fast find, retract, slow latch -- the slow number is kept.)
  #<z0> = #5422
  G38.2 Z[#<z0> - #<max_z>] F[#<f_fast>]
  o30 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G1 Z[#<z0>] F[#<f_trav>]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: no contact on the way down - is *87 clipped to the bar?)
  o30 endif
  G91
  G1 Z[#<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G38.2 Z[0.0 - [#<clear> * 2.0]] F[#<f_slow>]
  G90
  o31 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G1 Z[#<z0>] F[#<f_trav>]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: slow Z latch found nothing)
  o31 endif
  #<z_top> = #5063
  G1 Z[#<z_top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  (2. LEFT FLANK. Step X- by a full tool diameter so the tool clears the crown on)
  (the way down, then descend to the probe depth and come back at the bar.)
  #<x_start> = #5420
  G1 X[#<x_start> - #<t_dia>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G1 Z[#<z_top> - #<depth>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G38.2 X[#<x_start> + #<max_x>] F[#<f_fast>]
  o40 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G1 Z[#<z_top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
    G1 X[#<x_start>] F[#<f_trav>]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: left flank never touched)
  o40 endif
  #<xl_fast> = #5061
  G90
  G1 X[#<xl_fast> - #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G38.2 X[#<xl_fast> + #<clear>] F[#<f_slow>]
  o41 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G1 Z[#<z_top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: left flank slow latch found nothing)
  o41 endif
  #<x_left> = #5061
  G1 X[#<x_left> - #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  (3. RIGHT FLANK. Cross over ABOVE the bar, never through it: up to the crown)
  (clearance, across, then back down to the same probe depth.)
  G1 Z[#<z_top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  #<x_far> = [#<x_left> + #<t_dia> + [#<h> * 2.0] + #<clear>]
  G1 X[#<x_far>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G1 Z[#<z_top> - #<depth>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G38.2 X[#<x_far> - #<max_x>] F[#<f_fast>]
  o50 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G1 Z[#<z_top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: right flank never touched)
  o50 endif
  #<xr_fast> = #5061
  G90
  G1 X[#<xr_fast> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G38.2 X[#<xr_fast> - #<clear>] F[#<f_slow>]
  o51 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G1 Z[#<z_top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: right flank slow latch found nothing)
  o51 endif
  #<x_right> = #5061
  G1 X[#<x_right> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G1 Z[#<z_top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  (4. THE ANSWER. X is the mean of the two raw touches; Z is the crown less one)
  (bar radius. Both are in the CURRENT work frame, which is what G10 L20 wants.)
  #<x_axis> = [[#<x_left> + #<x_right>] / 2.0]
  #<z_axis> = [#<z_top> - #<r_bar>]
  (SANITY: the span the two touches saw must match the bar. Anything else means)
  (a touch landed on a chuck jaw, the fixture, or a burr -- and a bad datum here)
  (is silently wrong for every job after it.)
  #<span> = [#<x_right> - #<x_left> - #<t_dia>]
  #<span_err> = [ABS[#<span> - [#<h> * 2.0]]]
  o60 if [#<span_err> GT 1.0]
    (abort, ROTARY ZERO: flanks are %.3f#<span> apart, expected %.3f#<h> x2 - nothing set)
  o60 endif
  (5. SET IT. G10 L20 makes the CURRENT position read a value, so hand it the)
  (current position measured FROM the axis we just found.)
  G10 L20 P0 X[#5420 - #<x_axis>] Z[#5422 - #<z_axis>]
  (PRINT, ROTARY ZERO: X axis at %.4f#<x_axis>, crown %.4f#<z_top>, Z axis %.4f#<z_axis>, span err %.4f#<span_err>)
  (PRINT, ROTARY ZERO: X0 Z0 now sit on the B centreline - bar %.3f#<bar_dia> dia)
o<rotary_zero> endsub
M2 (end program)
